  "title": "Fano atoms are handles",
  "subject": "The closed surfaces of the knot's three-fold spaces: the orientable genus of their triangle-contact incidence graphs",
  "conclusion": "A three-fold space whose glue is planar has genus equal to its number of Fano atoms, because a piece that keeps its genus when a vertex is deleted adds exactly its genus across a three-edge splice, while in general such splices can lose handles. Its minimal maps are exactly connected sums of the chiral Heawood map, one per atom; the Fano plane's own map is the seven-vertex torus.",
